title: PLA
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Polylactic acid. A plastic made from plant sugars, usually corn or sugarcane, in place of oil.

It can be molded in the same machines as ordinary plastic.

It is compostable, with a catch. It needs the heat of an industrial composting facility. In a backyard pile or a landfill it mostly sits there.

Used in the [[Flax Chair]] and the [[Peel Chair]].
